[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

The digital version does not have any sorting method.&nbsp;

[/quote]

Good news! The digital version <strong>does</strong> have a three-option sorting method:&nbsp;tap/click on the "decks" icon in the upper-left, then&nbsp;select between "Alphabetical", "By Expansion", and "By Difficulty". Check it out:

[img]https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/alpha_sort.jpg[/img]

&nbsp;

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Though with all the content out now it’s possible they might rework the Multiverse Page. &nbsp;As to the Physcial dividers I’m not sure but with those ones you at least have the option of ordering them however you want. &nbsp;

[/quote]

Two important ports for clarity:

<ol>
	<li>I'm not talking about the <em>physical dividers</em>, I'm talking about the <em>published</em> listing in e.g. the Hero &amp; Villain Comparisons book (see left side of below image).</li>
	<li>I'm not talking about the digital game's <em>multiverse listing</em> (though, also a valid point of discussion) but about the <em>deck selection</em> interface (see right side of below image).&nbsp;</li>
</ol>

[img]https://greaterthangames.com/system/files/forum/attachments/alpha_sbs.jpg[/img]

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Per Christopher their full names are Void Guard &lt;name&gt; so that’s why they are listed in that order for the digital game. &nbsp;

[/quote]

[quote="Phantom5613"]

'Void Guard' is literally in the decks' name, so that's how they're sorted.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

Ultimately, whether "Void Guard" is part of Mainstay's name or not, whether "Indestructible" is part of Bunker's name or not, and whether including one or the other or both or neither as a factor in alphebetization is "correct" or not,&nbsp;the fact remains that there's a disparity between the published materials and the digital version.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

So far, it sounds like the answer to&nbsp;"Does anyone know if there's a way to get Sentinels Digital to sort heroes in the same alphabetical order that they're shown in the physical game (e.g. the Hero &amp; Villain Comparisons book)?" is either "No", or "Not without applying scissors and tape to your physical products."

&nbsp;

